## 3. Next.js Static Site Generation (SSG) — Pros & Cons

### How It Would Work

Remove `force-dynamic`, enable SSG/ISR. Pages pre-render at build time with JSON data baked in. On content change, trigger a rebuild or use ISR (Incremental Static Regeneration) to update specific pages.

### Pros

| Benefit | Details |
|---------|---------|
| ⚡ **Instant page loads** | HTML is pre-built, served from CDN edge. No server round-trip |
| 🚀 **No cold starts** | Static files don't need a running server |
| 💰 **Lower costs** | Static hosting (Cloud Storage + CDN) is cheaper than Cloud Run |
| 🌍 **Global performance** | CDN edge nodes worldwide vs. single Cloud Run region |
| 🔒 **Higher reliability** | No server to crash, no GCS outages affecting visitors |
| 📊 **Better Lighthouse scores** | Pre-rendered HTML = faster TTFB, better Core Web Vitals |

### Cons

| Tradeoff | Details |
|----------|---------|
| ⏱ **Content update delay** | Changes aren't instant. Full rebuild takes 1–3min, ISR revalidates in background |
| 🔧 **Build complexity** | Need GCS access at build time (already configured in `Dockerfile`) |
| 🔄 **Webhook/trigger needed** | Admin save → trigger rebuild or on-demand revalidation API |
| 🧩 **Dynamic features affected** | Contact form, price calculator still need client-side/API routes |
| 📦 **Build time scales** | More pages = longer builds (currently ~15 pages, manageable) |

### Can We Do It?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Yes, and it's relatively straightforward.** The codebase is 90% ready:
> - All content fetching is already in server components (page-level `readContent()`)
> - Dynamic parts (forms, calculators) are already client-side
> - Only change: remove `force-dynamic`, add `revalidate` export or ISR
> - Admin panel stays as a dynamic route (excluded from SSG)

### Recommended Approach: ISR (Incremental Static Regeneration)

```
Pages: SSG with revalidate: 3600 (1hr) or on-demand revalidation
Admin: stays force-dynamic (unchanged)
Rebuild trigger: admin save → call /api/revalidate → pages regenerate
```

This gives you static performance with near-instant content updates.

