## 7. Parallel Development & Safe Rollback Strategy

### Overview

The key insight: **both old and new admin panels read/write the same GCS JSON files.** This means they can coexist safely — the data layer is the shared contract.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Production (main branch)"
        A["/admin — Current JSON editor"]
    end
    subgraph "Development (feature branch)"
        B["/admin — New GUI editor"]
    end
    A -->|read/write| C["GCS: data/*.json"]
    B -->|read/write| C
    subgraph "Public Site (unchanged)"
        D["All pages read from GCS"]
    end
    D -->|readContent| C
```

### Git Branching Strategy

```
main ─────────────────────────────── (production, current admin)
  │
  └── feature/admin-v2 ──────────── (new admin, parallel dev)
         │
         ├── commit: scaffold GUI forms
         ├── commit: home-hero editor
         ├── commit: media browser
         └── ... (merge to main when ready)
```

**Rules:**
- `main` stays deployable at all times — current admin works
- `feature/admin-v2` branches from `main`, gets regular rebases
- New admin code lives under **the same `/admin` route** but on the branch
- No data migration needed — both versions use the same `readContent()` / `updateContent()`

### Development Setup

| Environment | Branch | URL | Purpose |
|-------------|--------|-----|---------|
| **Production** | `main` | `new.crisp-studio.com` | Live site + current admin |
| **Staging** | `feature/admin-v2` | `staging.crisp-studio.com` | New admin testing |
| **Local** | `feature/admin-v2` | `localhost:3000` | Development |

> [!TIP]
> **Staging option:** Deploy the feature branch to a second Cloud Run service (`crisp-website-staging`) pointing at the **same GCS bucket**. Both production and staging share data — edits in staging show up in production immediately.

If you want isolated staging, use a separate GCS prefix:
```
Production: data/*.json
Staging:    data-staging/*.json
```
Set via `DATA_PREFIX` env var (already configurable in `content.ts`).

### Rollback Safety Net

#### Layer 1: Git (instant rollback)

```bash
# If new admin has issues, revert to main
git checkout main
# Deploy main branch to Cloud Run
docker buildx build ... && gcloud run deploy ...
```

**Recovery time: ~5 minutes** (build + deploy).

#### Layer 2: Feature Flag (zero-downtime switch)

Add a simple env-var toggle so both admin versions exist in the same build:

```typescript
// In /admin/page.tsx
const USE_NEW_ADMIN = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_VERSION === 'v2';

export default function AdminPage() {
    if (USE_NEW_ADMIN) return <AdminV2Page />;
    return <AdminV1Page />;  // current JSON editor
}
```

**Rollback:** Change env var `ADMIN_VERSION=v1` and redeploy (or restart Cloud Run service). No code changes needed.

#### Layer 3: GCS Data Backup (content safety)

The existing `src/content/data/` git directory already serves as a backup. Strengthen it:

1. **Before each save**, the admin auto-commits JSON to `src/content/data/` (already exists)
2. **GCS versioning** — enable object versioning on the GCS bucket so every overwrite keeps the previous version
3. **Restore command**: `gsutil cp gs://bucket/data/filename.json#previous-version gs://bucket/data/filename.json`

```bash
# Enable GCS object versioning (one-time)
gsutil versioning set on gs://crisp-website-485112_cloudbuild
```

